Azure DevOps from scratch (and do it properly)… I wouldn’t chase every tool. I’d focus on Azure-native DevOps skills that real teams actually use. Here’s the roadmap I’d follow 

Phase 1 (Weeks 1–4): Core Foundations
Get solid before touching pipelines.
∟ Linux basics (processes, services, logs)
∟ Git fundamentals (branching, PRs, rebasing)
∟ Networking basics (DNS, ports, HTTP/S)
∟ Bash or Python for automation
∟ How applications run (not just “deploy button”)

Phase 2 (Weeks 5–8): Azure Fundamentals (Hands-on)
Not theory. Real Azure usage.
∟ Azure subscriptions, resource groups & regions
∟ Azure AD basics (users, service principals, RBAC)
∟ VMs vs App Services (when to use what)
∟ Storage Accounts (Blob, File, Queue — real use cases)
∟ Virtual Networks, subnets & NSGs
∟ Azure CLI (muscle memory)

Phase 3 (Weeks 9–12): Containers the Right Way
Containers before Kubernetes.
∟ Docker basics (images, layers, containers)
∟ Writing clean Dockerfiles
∟ Multi-stage builds
∟ Azure Container Registry (ACR)
∟ Run and debug containers locally
∟ Containerizing a real app (not hello-world)

Phase 4 (Weeks 13–16): Azure DevOps CI/CD
This is where DevOps actually starts.
∟ Azure Repos vs GitHub
∟ Azure DevOps Pipelines concepts
∟ YAML pipelines (build, test, artifacts)
∟ Pipeline triggers & environments
∟ Build & push Docker images to ACR
∟ Deploy to Azure App Service / VM from pipeline

Phase 5 (Weeks 17–20): Infrastructure as Code on Azure
Clicking in the portal doesn’t scale.
∟ Terraform fundamentals
∟ AzureRM provider
∟ Create VNets, VMs, App Services
∟ Remote state with Azure Storage
∟ Variables, outputs & modules
∟ Run Terraform via Azure DevOps pipeline

Phase 6 (Weeks 21–26): Kubernetes Fundamentals
Before AKS, understand Kubernetes itself.
∟ Pods, Deployments, ReplicaSets
∟ Services (ClusterIP, LoadBalancer)
∟ ConfigMaps & Secrets
∟ Resource requests & limits
∟ kubectl debugging
∟ Basic failure scenarios

Phase 7 (Weeks 27–32): Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)
Now connect Kubernetes to Azure.
∟ AKS architecture
∟ Node pools & scaling
∟ Integrating AKS with ACR
∟ Azure Load Balancer & Ingress
∟ Namespaces & RBAC
∟ Rolling updates & rollbacks

Phase 8 (Weeks 33–36): Observability & Reliability
DevOps = owning production.
∟ Azure Monitor & Log Analytics
∟ Application Insights
∟ Container & AKS logs
∟ Alerts (CPU, memory, failures)
∟ Basic SLI / SLO understanding

Phase 9 (Weeks 37–40): Azure DevOps Security
Security is not optional.
∟ Azure RBAC & least privilege
∟ Secure service connections
∟ Secrets with Key Vault
∟ Image vulnerability scanning
∟ AKS security basics
∟ Avoid common production mistakes

Phase 10 (Weeks 41–52): Real Azure DevOps Projects
This is what separates learners from engineers.
∟ End-to-end Azure infra with Terraform
∟ CI/CD for containerized apps
∟ AKS-based microservices
∟ Monitoring + alerts
∟ Break things → fix them → document
∟ Clear READMEs & architecture diagrams
